<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/706861bd049f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "This is, by the way, a test Microsoft says its Windows Hello Facial recognition technology reportedly didn't fail." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "444" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/18bb717a61d9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "When Apple announced its $1k iPhone X back in September, we learned they were ditching the home screen button log-in for something snazzier: facial recognition." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "442" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4f35e14ac319> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "This is Apple's attempt at conquering biometric security, and it could be either a huge success or a giant letdown." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "446" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ccc2af9dd853> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "As noted by 9to5Mac, Apple has stated that Face ID is an even more secure way to unlock an iPhone than Touch ID was, with there being a one in 1,000,000 chance of a different person being able to dupe its facial recognition software." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "445" .

